===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|sūgan||to suck}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*sūganą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*sug-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*suk-}}. Compare Low German {{m|nds|sugen}}, Dutch {{m|nl|zuigen}}, Danish {{m|da|suge}}.

====Verb====
{{de-verb-strong|class=2|saugt|sog|gesogen|past subjunctive=söge}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[suck]]; to create underpressure with a tube-like object such as one's mouth
#: {{ux|de|an etwas '''saugen'''|t=to suck on something|inline=1}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[suck]] (something)
# {{lb|de|colloquial|transitive}} to [[download]] something

